                "word": "shyster",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "732585d5-0f41-4878-a0e3-aef6f801b878",
                        "entry_id": "0df256a7-f10c-3fbb-9bd4-e4ca0706240f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "shysters"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "311cfeba-f983-34f7-8018-667f3acf6955",
                        "entry_id": "0df256a7-f10c-3fbb-9bd4-e4ca0706240f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone who acts in a disreputable, unethical, or unscrupulous way, especially in the practice of law and politics."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3c6c2485-a39b-4fd5-b300-1e42cb5da435",
                                "sense_id": "311cfeba-f983-34f7-8018-667f3acf6955",
                                "text": "True, it was a good advertisement at Boosters' Club lunches, and all the varieties of Annual Banquets to which Good Fellows were invited, to speak sonorously of […] a thing called Ethics, whose nature was confusing but if you had it you were a High-class Realtor and if you hadn't you were a shyster, a piker, and a fly-by-night."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "07210c20-331e-4f6e-88fb-4320b9bcd863",
                                "sense_id": "311cfeba-f983-34f7-8018-667f3acf6955",
                                "text": "The network canceled—nonco-operation their legal shysters said. Suing me, for, for ten million clams, damages to sponsors, agencies. Internal Revenue-Uncle Whiskers says I owe them a mint."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "72bf798c-06e7-48ce-97b5-cba430794c0e",
                                "sense_id": "311cfeba-f983-34f7-8018-667f3acf6955",
                                "text": "I could sue you, Polly. A shyster is a disreputable lawyer. I'm a quack."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ddfa498c-b5e4-4c4f-b2f2-3037cfe322e0",
                        "source_entry_id": "0df256a7-f10c-3fbb-9bd4-e4ca0706240f",
                        "source_sense_id": "311cfeba-f983-34f7-8018-667f3acf6955",
                        "source_sense_description": "someone who acts in a disreputable, unethical, or unscrupulous way",
                        "target_lang_word": "avocaillon",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "avocaillon",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ffe845ba-586a-36ed-bc76-5691360c0836",
                                        "entry_id": "ad0ddac2-59f8-378d-97e4-221cb0ab2f14",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Avocat minable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "pejorative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c8c928c-0c97-46e4-a621-9f927867e5fa",
                                                "sense_id": "ffe845ba-586a-36ed-bc76-5691360c0836",
                                                "text": "Contrarié, vexé, M. de Poyanne fit une scène à Agate, lui reprocha de se mésallier : ce garçon n’était qu’un butor, un avocaillon vide et bruyant, qui plus est le rejeton d’un obscur hobereau de province."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2da35cc4-9d8d-402b-b414-70ce29b82b44",
                                                "sense_id": "ffe845ba-586a-36ed-bc76-5691360c0836",
                                                "text": "— Et si tu fermes pas ta grand’ gueule d’avocaillon d’la mer, continua Mr. Pike, j’te f’rai sortir d’ici à coups de pied, et tu verras c’que c’est d’travailler…\n— J’aurai des dommages et intérêts, ricana Davis.\n— Pas si j’t’ai enterré avant, répliqua du tac au tac le second, menaçant ; et laisse-moi t’dire, Davis, qu’tu s’ras pas l’premier avocaillon d’la mer qu’j’aurai fait balancer par d’ssus bord avec un sac d’charbon aux pieds.\nMr. Pike tourna les talons sur un « sacré foutu avocaillon d’la mer ! » et il reprit le chemin de la passerelle à grands pas."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7dbfed70-7c4f-423e-92de-e5d453b4a7d7",
                        "source_entry_id": "0df256a7-f10c-3fbb-9bd4-e4ca0706240f",
                        "source_sense_id": "311cfeba-f983-34f7-8018-667f3acf6955",
